105504_b185","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"45","DOI":"10.1080\/13504860210132879","article-title":"Basics of electricity derivative pricing in competitive markets","volume":"9","author":"Vehvil\u00e4inen","year":"2002","journal-title":"Appl. Math. Finance"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b186","series-title":"Stochastics of Environmental and Financial Economics","first-page":"321","article-title":"Modelling the impact of wind power production on electricity prices by regime-switching L\u00e9vy semistationary processes","author":"Veraart","year":"2016"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b187","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Villaplana, P., 2003. Pricing power derivatives: A two-factor jump-diffusion approach. In: EFMA 2004 Basel Meetings Paper.","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.493943"},{"issue":"2","key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b188","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.5547\/01956574.35.2.3","article-title":"Residual demand modeling and application to electricity pricing","volume":"35","author":"Wagner","year":"2014","journal-title":"Energy J."},{"issue":"5","key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b189","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"453","DOI":"10.1080\/1350486X.2020.1715808","article-title":"Polynomial processes for power prices","volume":"26","author":"Ware","year":"2019","journal-title":"Appl. Math. Finance"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b190","series-title":"Identifying Risk Factors and Their Premia: A Study on Electricity Prices","author":"Wei","year":"2020"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b191","unstructured":"Weron, R., 2005. Heavy tails and electricity prices. In: The Deutsche Bundesbanks 2005 Annual Fall Conference (Eltville)."},{"issue":"4","key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b192","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1030","DOI":"10.1016\/j.ijforecast.2014.08.008","article-title":"Electricity price forecasting: A review of the state-of-the-art with a look into the future","volume":"30","author":"Weron","year":"2014","journal-title":"Int. J. Forecast."},{"issue":"1\u20132","key":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504_b193","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"39","DOI":"10.1016\/j.physa.2004.01.008","article-title":"Modeling electricity prices: jump diffusion and regime switching","volume":"336","author":"Weron","year":"2004","journal-title":"Physica A"}],"container-title":["Energy Economics"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0140988321003881?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0140988321003881?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,26]],"date-time":"2025-09-26T01:21:31Z","timestamp":1758849691000},"score":74.61211,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/S0140988321003881"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2021,10]]},"references-count":193,"alternative-id":["S0140988321003881"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504","ISSN":["0140-9883"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0140-9883","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2021,10]]},"assertion":[{"value":"Elsevier","name":"publisher","label":"This article is maintained by"},{"value":"A survey of electricity spot and futures price models for risk management applications","name":"articletitle","label":"Article Title"},{"value":"Energy Economics","name":"journaltitle","label":"Journal Title"},{"value":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.eneco.2021.105504","name":"articlelink","label":"CrossRef DOI link to publisher maintained version"},{"value":"article","name":"content_type","label":"Content Type"},{"value":"\u00a9 2021 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","name":"copyright","label":"Copyright"}],"article-number":"105504"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,12]],"date-time":"2026-08-12T09:33:31Z","timestamp":1786527211554,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2012]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":76,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>We examine the dependence structure of electricity spot prices across regional markets in Australia. One of the major objectives in establishing a national electricity market was to provide a nationally integrated and efficient electricity market, limiting market power of generators in the separate regional markets. Our analysis is based on a GARCH approach to model the marginal price series in the considered regions in combination with copulae to capture the dependence structure between the marginals. We apply different copula models including Archimedean, elliptical and copula mixture models. We find a positive dependence structure between the prices for all considered markets, while the strongest dependence is exhibited between markets that are connected via interconnector transmission lines. Regarding the nature of dependence, the Student-t copula provides a good fit to the data, while the overall best results are obtained using copula mixture models due to their ability to also capture asymmetric dependence in the tails of the distribution. Interestingly, our results also suggest that for the four major markets, NSW, QLD, SA and VIC, the degree of dependence has decreased starting from the year 2008 towards the end of the sample period in 2010. Examining the Value-at-Risk of stylized portfolios constructed from electricity spot contracts in different markets, we find that the Student-t and mixture copula models outperform the Gaussian copula in a backtesting study. Our results are important for risk management and hedging decisions of market participants, in particular for those operating in several regional markets simultaneously.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.1991452","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2012,1,25]],"date-time":"2012-01-25T11:57:57Z","timestamp":1327492677000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Modeling Spot Price Dependence in Australian Electricity Markets with Applications to Risk Management"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Katja","family":"Ignatieva","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5302-3850","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Stefan","family":"Trueck","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","reference":[{"issue":"6","key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"716","DOI":"10.1109\/tac.1974.1100705","article-title":"A new look at the statistical model identification","volume":"19","author":"H Akaike","year":"1974","journal-title":"IEEE Transaction on Automatic Control"},{"key":"ref2","article-title":"Potential generator market power in the NEM, rule determination, final rule determination","year":"2013","journal-title":"Australian Energy Market Commission"},{"key":"ref3","year":"2010","journal-title":"An introduction to australia's national electricity market"},{"key":"ref4","year":"2015","journal-title":"Wholesale statistics: Annual interregional trade as a percentage of regional energy consumption"},{"key":"ref5","year":"2013","journal-title":"Australian Government Productivity Commission"},{"key":"ref6","author":"O Barndorff-Nielsen","year":"1995","journal-title":"Normal-inverse Gaussian processes and the modelling of stock returns"},{"key":"ref7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1142\/6811","author":"F Benth","year":"2008","journal-title":"Stochastic Modeling of Electricity and Related Markets"},{"key":"ref8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1347","DOI":"10.1111\/1540-6261.00463","article-title":"Equilibrium pricing and optimal hedging in electricity forward markets","volume":"57","author":"H Bessembinder","year":"2