title":"Modeling highly volatile and seasonal markets: Evidence from the Nord Pool electricity market"},{"issue":"2","key":"ref74","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"337","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2003.11.002","article-title":"Transmission of prices and price volatility in Australian electricity spot markets: A multivariate garch analysis","volume":"27","author":"A Worthington","year":"2005","journal-title":"Energy Economics"},{"issue":"5","key":"ref75","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1080\/03610910701539781","article-title":"Simulating from exchangeable archimedean copulas","volume":"36","author":"F Wu","year":"2007","journal-title":"Communications in Statistics -Simulation and Computation"},{"key":"ref76","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2007.07.002","volume":"30","author":"G Zachmann","year":"2008","journal-title":"Electricity wholesale market prices in Europe: Convergence? Energy Economics"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,12]],"date-time":"2026-08-12T08:55:49Z","timestamp":1786524949000},"score":40.914642,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=1991452"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2012]]},"references-count":76,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.1991452","published":{"date-parts":[[2012]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,23]],"date-time":"2026-09-23T17:16:51Z","timestamp":1790183811732,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":53,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"18","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,10]],"date-time":"2020-09-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1599696000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Energies"],"abstract":"<jats:p>In dealing with sharp changes in electricity prices, contract planning is considered as a vital risk management tool for stakeholders in deregulated power markets. In this paper, dynamics of spot prices in Turkish electricity market are analyzed, and predictive performance of several models are compared, i.e., time series models and regime-switching models. Different models for derivative pricing are proposed, and alternative portfolio optimization problems using mean-variance optimization and conditional value at risk (CVaR) are solved. Expected payoff and risk structure for different hedging strategies for a hypothetical electricity company with a given demand are analyzed. Experimental studies show that regime-switching models are able to capture electricity characteristics better than their standard counterparts. In addition, evaluations with various risk management models demonstrate that those models are highly competent in providing an effective risk control practice for electricity markets.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/en13184698","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,10]],"date-time":"2020-09-10T09:10:09Z","timestamp":1599729009000},"page":"4698","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":14,"title":["Comparison of Electricity Spot Price Modelling and Risk Management Applications"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"13","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2572-1985","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ethem","family":"\u00c7anako\u011flu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Industrial Engineering Department, Bah\u00e7e\u015fehir University Be\u015fikta\u015f, Istanbul 34353, Turkey"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Esra","family":"Ad\u0131yeke","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Industrial Engineering Department, Bah\u00e7e\u015fehir University Be\u015fikta\u015f, Istanbul 34353, Turkey"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,10]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"111","DOI":"10.21314\/JEM.2009.021","article-title":"The information premium for non-storable commodities","volume":"2","author":"Benth","year":"2009","journal-title":"J. Energy Mark."},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"5","DOI":"10.1023\/A:1013846631785","article-title":"Electricity Prices and Power Derivatives: Evidence from the Nordic Power Exchange","volume":"5","author":"Lucia","year":"2002","journal-title":"Rev. Deriv. Res."},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"96","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2013.03.013","article-title":"Identifying spikes and seasonal components in electricity spot price data: A guide to robust modeling","volume":"38","author":"Janczura","year":"2013","journal-title":"Energy Econ."},{"key":"ref_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Weber, C. (2004). Uncertainty in the Electric Power Industry: Methods and Models for Decision Support, Springer.","DOI":"10.1007\/b100484"},{"key":"ref_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"435","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2016.08.008","article-title":"Electricity price forecasting using sale and purchase curves: The X-Model","volume":"59","author":"Ziel","year":"2016","journal-title":"Energy Econ."},{"key":"ref_6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"251","DOI":"10.1016\/j.rser.2018.05.038","article-title":"Probabilistic mid-and long-term electricity price forecasting","volume":"94","author":"Ziel","year":"2018","journal-title":"Renew. Sustain. Energy Rev."},{"key":"ref_7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"242","DOI":"10.1002\/for.2624","article-title":"Forecasting of electricity price through a functional prediction of sale and purchase curves","volume":"39","author":"Shah","year":"2020","journal-title":"J. Forecast."},{"key":"ref_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Bower, J., and Bunn, D.W. (2000). Model-based comparisons of pool and bilateral markets for electricity. Energy J., 21.","DOI":"10.5547\/ISSN0195-6574-EJ-Vol21-No3-1"},{"key":"ref_9","doi-asse