nal-title":"J. Am. Stat. Assoc."},{"key":"ref_44","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"987","DOI":"10.2307\/1912773","article-title":"Autoregressive Conditional Heteroscedasticity with Estimates of the Variance of United Kingdom Inflation","volume":"50","author":"Engle","year":"1982","journal-title":"Econometrica"},{"key":"ref_45","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"425","DOI":"10.1016\/S0140-9883(03)00041-0","article-title":"Regime jumps in electricity prices","volume":"25","author":"Huisman","year":"2003","journal-title":"Energy Econ."},{"key":"ref_46","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"622","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1468-0084.2011.00632.x","article-title":"Modelling Electricity Prices: International Evidence","volume":"73","author":"Escribano","year":"2011","journal-title":"Oxf. Bull. Econ. Stat."},{"key":"ref_47","unstructured":"Deng, S. (2000, January 4\u20137). Pricing electricity derivatives under alternative stochastic spot price models. Proceedings of the 33rd Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences, Maui, HI, USA."},{"key":"ref_48","first-page":"77","article-title":"Portfolio Selection","volume":"7","author":"Markowitz","year":"1952","journal-title":"J. Financ."},{"key":"ref_49","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"169","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2008.08.003","article-title":"Electricity portfolio management: Optimal peak\/off-peak allocations","volume":"31","author":"Huisman","year":"2009","journal-title":"Energy Econ."},{"key":"ref_50","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"203","DOI":"10.1111\/1467-9965.00068","article-title":"Coherent measures of risk","volume":"9","author":"Artzner","year":"1999","journal-title":"Math. Financ."},{"key":"ref_51","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"21","DOI":"10.21314\/JOR.2000.038","article-title":"Optimization of Conditional Value-at-Risk","volume":"2","author":"Rockafellar","year":"2000","journal-title":"J. Risk"},{"key":"ref_52","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Maggioni, F., and Allevi, E. (2017, January 4\u20137). Bounding Multistage Stochastic Programs: A Scenario Tree Based Approach. Proceedings of the International Conference on Optimization and Decision Science, Sorrento, Italy.","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-319-67308-0_41"},{"key":"ref_53","unstructured":"Lofberg, J. (2004, January 2\u20134). YALMIP: A toolbox for modeling and optimization in MATLAB. Proceedings of the 2004 IEEE International Symposium on Computer Aided Control Systems Design, New Orleans, LA, USA."}],"container-title":["Energies"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.mdpi.com\/1996-1073\/13\/18\/4698\/pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,11]],"date-time":"2025-10-11T10:08:31Z","timestamp":1760177311000},"score":39.176006,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.mdpi.com\/1996-1073\/13\/18\/4698"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,10]]},"references-count":53,"journal-issue":{"issue":"18","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,9]]}},"alternative-id":["en13184698"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/en13184698","ISSN":["1996-1073"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1996-1073","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2020,9,10]]}},{"institution":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/013cjyk83","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Paris Sciences et Lettres (ComUE)"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T17:52:59Z","timestamp":1791309179842,"version":"4.3.1"},"reference-count":112,"publisher":"Agence Bibliographique de l'Enseignement Sup\u00e9rieur","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:title>Mod\u00e9lisation de la d\u00e9pendance entre processus stochastiques en temps continu : une application aux march\u00e9s de l'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9 et \u00e0 la gestion des risques<\/jats:title>\n                <jats:p xml:lang=\"fr\">Cette th\u00e8se traite de probl\u00e8mes de d\u00e9pendance entre processus stochastiques en temps continu. Ces r\u00e9sultats sont appliqu\u00e9s \u00e0 la mod\u00e9lisation et \u00e0 la gestion des risques des march\u00e9s de l'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9.Dans une premi\u00e8re partie, de nouvelles copules sont \u00e9tablies pour mod\u00e9liser la d\u00e9pendance entre deux mouvements Browniens et contr\u00f4ler la distribution de leur diff\u00e9rence. On montre que la classe des copules admissibles pour les Browniens contient des copules asym\u00e9triques. Avec ces copules, la fonction de survie de la diff\u00e9rence des deux Browniens est plus \u00e9lev\u00e9e dans sa partie positive qu'avec une d\u00e9pendance gaussienne. Les r\u00e9sultats sont appliqu\u00e9s \u00e0 la mod\u00e9lisation jointe des prix de l'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9 et d'autres commodit\u00e9s \u00e9nerg\u00e9tiques. Dans une seconde partie, nous consid\u00e9rons un processus stochastique observ\u00e9 de mani\u00e8re discr\u00e8te et d\u00e9fini par la somme d'une semi-martingale continue et d'un processus de Poisson compos\u00e9 avec retour \u00e0 la moyenne. Une proc\u00e9dure d'estimation pour le param\u00e8tre de retour \u00e0 la moyenne est propos\u00e9e lorsque celui-ci est \u00e9lev\u00e9 dans un cadre de statistique haute fr\u00e9quence en horizon fini. Ces r\u00e9sultats sont utilis\u00e9s pour la mod\u00e9lisation des pics dans les prix de l'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9.Dans une troisi\u00e8me partie, on consid\u00e8re un processus de Poisson doublement stochastique dont l'intensit\u00e9 stochastique est une fonction d'une semi-martingale continue. Pour estimer cette fonction, un estimateur \u00e0 polyn\u00f4mes locaux est utilis\u00e9 et une m\u00e9thode de s\u00e9lection de la fen\u00eatre est propos\u00e9e menant \u00e0 une in\u00e9galit\u00e9 oracle. Un test est propos\u00e9 pour d\u00e9terminer si la fonction d'intensit\u00e9 appartient \u00e0 une certaine famille param\u00e9trique. Gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 ces r\u00e9sultats, on mod\u00e9lise la d\u00e9pendance entre l'intensit\u00e9 des pics de prix de l'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9 et de facteurs exog\u00e8nes tels que la production \u00e9olienne.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.70675\/a3382ce9z418bz47f3z908fz88fd42b539b0","type":"dissertation","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,2]],"date-time":"2026-04-02T16:47:54Z","timestamp":1775148474000},"approved":{"date-parts":[[2017,12,8]]},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Dependence modeling between continuous time stochastic processes : an application to electricity markets modeling and risk management"],"prefix":"10.70675","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7532-0848","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Thomas","family":"Deschatre","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/013cjyk83","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Paris Sciences et Lettres (ComUE)"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"51494","reference":[{"key":"96416_160_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Benth Fred Espen, Kallsen Jan, Meyer-Brandis Thilo, A non-gaussian ornstein-uhlenbeck process for electricity spot price modeling and derivatives pricing, in: Applied Mathematical Finance, vol. 14, n\u00b0 2, p. 153-169, 2007","DOI":"10.1080\/13504860600725031","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_60_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Benth Fred Espen, Kettler Paul C, Dynamic copula models for the spark spread, in: Quantitative Finance, vol. 11, n\u00b0 3, p. 407-421, 2011","DOI":"10.1080\/14697688.2010.481629","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_198_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Chen Feng, Yip Paul SF, Lam KF, On the local polynomial estimators of the counting process intensity function and its derivatives, in: Scandinavian Journal of Statistics, vol. 38, n\u00b0 4, p. 631-649, 2011","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1467-9469.2011.00733.x","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_87_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"R\u00fcschendorf Ludger, Random variables with maximum sums, in: Advances in Applied Probability, p. 623-632, 1982","DOI":"10.2307\/1426677","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_198_11","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Cont Rama, Tankov Peter, Financial modelling with jump processes, volume 2, CRC press, 2003","DOI":"10.1201\/9780203485217","type":"book"},{"key":"96416_86_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Carmona Ren\u00e9, Durrleman Valdo, Generalizing the black-scholes formula to multivariate contingent claims, in: Journal of computational finance, vol. 9, n\u00b0 2, p. 43, 2005","DOI":"10.21314\/JCF.2005.159","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_114_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Benth Fred Espen, Koekebakker Steen, Stochastic modeling of financial electricity contracts, in: Energy Economics, vol. 30, n\u00b0 3, p. 1116-1157, 2008","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eneco.2007.06.005","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_161_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Mancini Cecilia, Estimation of the characteristics of the jumps of a general poisson-diffusion model, in: Scandinavian Actuarial Journal, vol. 2004, n\u00b0 1, p. 42-52, 2004","DOI":"10.1080\/034612303100170091","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_199_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Meyer-Brandis Thilo, Tankov Peter, Multi-factor jump-diffusion models of electricity prices, in: International Journal of Theoretical and Applied Finance, vol. 11, n\u00b0 05, p. 503-528, 2008","DOI":"10.1142\/S0219024908004907","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_223_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Veraart Almut Elisabeth Dorothea, Inference for the jump part of quadratic variation of It\u00f4 semimartingales, in: Econometric Theory, vol. 26, n\u00b0 2, p. 331-368, 2010","DOI":"10.1017\/S0266466609100014","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"96416_61_10","unstructured":"Crane Glenis, Time and space varying copulas, 2008, arXiv preprint arXiv:081